{
  "_": "The Modules tab's shelves, built like the Tools tab. `polcok` lists the shelves in display order: a name in each of the app's 15 languages, the SF Symbol of the heading, and the module ids on it in the order they are meant to be met. `modulok` is each module's tile: an SF Symbol, a palette colour (purple, indigo, blue, cyan, teal, mint, green, yellow, orange, red, pink, brown, gray) and a short caption in hu/en/ro (other languages fall back to English). The caption leans on its shelf — on the remote-viewing shelf 'Advanced' is enough — and keeps the teacher's name where that is how the module is known. build-everything copies this file into everything.json as `modulPolcok`. To add a module: put its id on one shelf, where it belongs in the order (recordings and links right after their course), and give it a row under `modulok` with a symbol that exists on iOS 17.0. A module on no shelf still installs; the app shows it on an 'Other' shelf with the default icon.",
